Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: zino
Comment:
 Ritz is the Tcl/Tk client of the Zino network monitoring suite, developed by
 UNINETT, now part of Sikt. The source package is the whole Zino suite; only
 the ritz/ subtree and a generated version.tcl are used to build the binary
 package.
 .
 Most files in the tree carry no licence header at all. Sikt, as the copyright
 holder, states that the suite is BSD licensed. The files that do carry a
 header disagree with one another: 43 use the four-clause form and 9 use the
 three-clause form. The split is chronological rather than deliberate. The
 four-clause files date from 1996 to 1999 and the three-clause files from 2001
 to 2010, which matches the industry-wide move away from the advertising
 clause after Berkeley retired it in 1999. They are documented separately here
 rather than flattened to a single licence, because relabelling a file is not
 ours to do. Sikt intends to consolidate this in a later version.
 .
 Note that ritz/just/justSNMP.tcl carries the four-clause form and is
 concatenated into the generated /usr/bin/ritz, so the advertising clause
 currently applies to the ritz binary package.
 .
 Upstream has no public repository: it is maintained in a private git
 repository at Sikt, converted from the original CVS history.

